    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present this 2-bedroom terrace family home to the Dublin 10 property market. Positioned on the mature and highly sought-after Drumfinn Avenue, No. 113 offers c. 74 sqm of well-proportioned living space. Presenting a fantastic opportunity for first-time buyers, savvy renovators, or investors looking to acquire a solid property with immense potential in a proven residential location, No. 113 is in need of complete modernization throughout.\nThe location is second to none. Drumfinn Avenue is ideally situated within easy walking distance of Ballyfermot Village, offering a wealth of local amenities including primary and secondary schools, local shops, supermarkets, sports clubs, and cafes. The idyllic green spaces of Markievicz Park and Phoenix Park are both close by. Public transport connections are exceptional, with prime bus corridors providing swift, direct access into Dublin City Centre, while the Luas Red Line, Park West Train Station, and the M50/N7 motorways are all easily accessible by car.\nInternal living accommodation of c. 74 sqm features well-proportioned rooms over two floors. Downstairs comprises a welcoming entrance hallway, a spacious front living room, a large open-plan kitchen and dining area to the rear, and a main family bathroom suite situated at the back. Upstairs features two generous double bedrooms. To the rear, the property boasts a private garden with excellent potential for further extension (subject to necessary planning permission).\n. Viewing is highly advised, call RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS today for further information or to arrange a viewing!\nAdditional Features;\n•c. 74 sqm\n•BER E\n•2 BED / 2 BATH\n•In need of modernization throughout — fantastic potential\n•Large kitchen/dining room to the rear\n•Bright front living room\n•Main family bathroom located to the rear\n•Two generous bedrooms \n•Excellent opportunity to extend to the rear (subject to p.p.)\n•Private rear garden\n•Quiet, mature, and highly popular residential road\n•Short walk to Ballyfermot Village, local schools & Markievicz Park\n•Prime public transport links into Dublin City Centre\n•Easy access to Luas Red Line, M50 & N7 motorways\n•Ideal for First-Time Buyers, Renovators, and Investors\nDirections\nFrom the Red Cow Roundabout, proceed onto the Naas Road inbound toward Dublin City Centre. Turn left at the major junction onto Kylemore Road and continue straight towards Ballyfermot. At the main junction, turn left onto Ballyfermot Road. Take a right turn onto Drumfinn Road, then take your next left onto Drumfinn Avenue. Continue straight along the road, and No. 113 will be located on your right-hand side, clearly identified by our Ray Cooke Auctioneers 'For Sale' sign.\n"
      },
      {
